      "title": "Australia’s housing prices are trending down. See which suburbs have had the biggest falls",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/05/house-prices-trending-down-sydney-melbourne-brisbane-perth-darwin",
      "description": "<p>Cotality says prices have declined in most capital cities over winter. Search the data to see how they have changed in your area</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s property market is facing a rare price correction, as rising interest rates and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/13/property-investors-australia-tax-negative-gearing-rba-interest-rates\">less favourable tax settings for investors</a> accelerate a downturn.</p><p>Most capital cities recorded winter price falls, according to Cotality data, with Sydney leading the decline. That weakness is expected to continue, as higher inflation could lead to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/02/property-house-prices-drop-sydney-melbourne-brisbane-perth-adelaide-interest-rates\">further interest rate hikes</a>, denting demand.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/05/house-prices-trending-down-sydney-melbourne-brisbane-perth-darwin\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-04T15:00:12"
    },
    {
      "title": "Charles Perrottet denies asking brother as premier to appoint cabinet minister, Icac hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/04/charles-perrottet-denies-asking-premier-brother-to-appoint-cabinet-minister-icac-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Charles says claims by developer Jean Nassif in an intercepted phone call that ‘we’re reshuffling the government’ did not reflect promises allegedly made to Nassif</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/04/anthony-albanese-pauline-hanson-actu-union-labor-one-nation-coalition-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The younger brother of Dominic Perrottet has denied asking his brother to appoint a cabinet minister to achieve outcomes for a property developer, a corruption inquiry has heard.</p><p>Charles Perrottet told the Independent Commission Against Corruption (Icac) on Friday that claims made in an intercepted phone call featuring developer Jean Nassif days before his brother became the NSW premier – in which Nassif described Dominic Perrottet as “my boy” – did not reflect promises allegedly made to Nassif.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/04/charles-perrottet-denies-asking-premier-brother-to-appoint-cabinet-minister-icac-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-04T06:28:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "EV sales outpace petrol cars for first time as Australians dodge soaring fuel costs",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/04/ev-sales-outpace-petrol-cars-for-first-time-as-australians-dodge-soaring-fuel-costs",
      "description": "<p>New record for Australia as more than 27,000 EVs sold in August, driven by the rising cost of fuel and new government policy</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/04/anthony-albanese-pauline-hanson-actu-union-labor-one-nation-coalition-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Electric vehicle sales in Australia exceeded petrol cars for the first time last month as a transformation driven by high fuel prices and government policy encouraging clean car uptake accelerated.</p><p>More than 27,000 EVs were sold in August, a new record for a single month and representing 24.9% of new cars sold. The climate-friendly technology surpassed both petrol vehicles (nearly 26,000 sold) and diesel cars (23,600).</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/04/ev-sales-outpace-petrol-cars-for-first-time-as-australians-dodge-soaring-fuel-costs\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-04T03:26:43"
    }
